      "path": "theories/shengsheng-buxi-generative-existence/unified-2026-10-05/MATHEMATICAL-ROOT-FRONTIER.md",
      "block": "## Dependent domains and the whole-family boundary\n\n7 October 2026. [The integrated continuation](../../../_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/ROOT-MATHEMATICAL-FAMILIES-INTEGRATION.md) adds **33 checked theorems and 52 declaration audits**. Finite bases with finite fibers have finite dependent-pair and section domains; empty, singleton and binary-union admission at those carriers suffice for full predicate admission. For arbitrary supplied families, total functional finite-graph ideals represent complete sections, with fixed-base fiber correspondence preserving evaluation and predicate membership.\n\nThe new boundary is exact: admitting supports of every ambient family of finite—or merely subsingleton—fibers is equivalent to full predicate admission. Arbitrary empty/singleton assignments already carry the target predicate. Thus local smallness does not independently justify the whole assignment. One section's classical existence is also distinct from admitting the complete section space.\n\nThis is domain-level coverage, without a dependent object-language truth theorem, base-changing family semantics or internal universes. The affirmative argument, independent internal review and primary-source comparison support testing a meaning-based warrant for collective inductive formation next. Independent infinite-domain admission, universal coverage and exclusive constitutive priority remain unresolved.\n\n",
      "block_sha256": "b443482cab10862b8661a6531b11774ae6eb91d5093bd31c720e24188237ed32",
      "before_sha256": "fc42bccaf720ec58e909edb834c47fd700fb0167d94cf9266369e034b21c2910",
      "after_sha256": "f696c676ca20cd7698904e6135ab88e44409bacebcb07c055316be8631d50d43",
      "preserved_prior_bytes_at_write": true
    },
    {
      "path": "sources/15-codex-theory-conversations/2026-10-07-mathematical-admission-and-coverage.md",
      "block": "## Subsequent continuation\n\nAfter the finite-admission and named-theory results, Ren requested:\n\n> please continue\n\nThe [dependent-family continuation](../../_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/ROOT-MATHEMATICAL-FAMILIES-INTEGRATION.md) is the AI-authored response. It extends finite dependent-domain admission and graph reconstruction, tests the strength of arbitrary finite-fiber support admission, and keeps the two universal obligations unfinished. The choice of this next formal test and the proposed collective-induction investigation are AI-authored, not quotations from Ren.\n\n",
      "block_sha256": "f0f0fc1d634895cf334bca9ca99e51144435dd0b2c909964dfa137b01ca36f19",
